{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSDkhZ5NGZUtVVkk9QZW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The new tests fail against the old code and all 4 pass with the fix. Now ANSWER.md:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2004,"cache_read_input_tokens":24575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2004},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d8ba11-6068-4a90-8ad8-f7dd4035c154","uuid":"9cdbbe0a-de52-4169-b43c-cba00ae244ce","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:52:00.503Z","request_id":"req_011CgSDkhCjiz9fkynwCEpdk"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSDkhZ5NGZUtVVkk9QZW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MTS9yWqbkz76qWxhytbtD2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-gt0pAp/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story with `similar: [{slug, score}]`, and the score\ncame from `similarity()`, which returned `round(0.7 * tag + 0.3 * word, 4)`.\nThat is a Python **float**. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats anywhere\nin an item:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n(see `logs/error.log`, raised from `table.put_item` in `publish`).\n\n- **First publish:** the table is empty, so `similar == []` and the item has no\n  floats. It succeeds (`similar=0 stored`, 201).\n- **Every later publish:** there is now at least one existing story, so\n  `similar` has a float `score`. `put_item` raises `TypeError`, and `handler`\n  turns that into a 500.\n\nThe only test published a single story into an empty table, so it never\nexercised a non-empty `similar` list.\n\n## Fix (`src/app.py`)\n\n1. **At the source:** `similarity()` now returns\n   `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`. Going through `str` gives an exact 4-place\n   decimal such as `Decimal('0.4429')`, not the float's binary expansion.\n   Sorting and comparing still work as before.\n2. **At the write boundary, so it can't come back:** a new `to_dynamo()` helper\n   recursively converts any float to `Decimal`, and `publish()` sends the item\n   through it right before `put_item`. A float added to the item later (a new\n   field, a changed formula) gets converted instead of causing another 500.\n\n## Regression tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_float_free_scores`: publishes two related\n  stories and checks the second one stores with a non-empty `similar`. This is\n  the exact production failure.\n- `test_handler_returns_201_for_every_publish`: five publishes through\n  `handler`, and each one must return 201.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_nested_floats`: checks the boundary helper on\n  nested dicts and lists.\n\n`tests/fake_dynamo.py` already rejects floats the same way boto3 does. Before\nthe fix the new tests fail with that `TypeError`; after it, all 4 tests pass\n(`python3 -m unittest discover tests`).\n\n## Side note (not the cause of this bug)\n\n`table.scan()` returns at most 1 MB per call, and `publish` doesn't follow\n`LastEvaluatedKey`. Once the library is large, `similar` will be computed from\nonly part of it. This won't cause a 500, but it's worth paginating (or\nprecomputing) later.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2004,"cache_read_input_tokens":24575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2004},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d8ba11-6068-4a90-8ad8-f7dd4035c154","uuid":"0ffe189a-7c14-4d48-9c12-68a21aa92427","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:52:09.014Z","request_id":"req_011CgSDkhCjiz9fkynwCEpdk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MTS9yWqbkz76qWxhytbtD2":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-gt0pAp/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story with `similar: [{slug, score}]`, and the score\ncame from `similarity()`, which returned `round(0.7 * tag + 0.3 * word, 4)`.\nThat is a Python **float**. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats anywhere\nin an item:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n(see `logs/error.log`, raised from `table.put_item` in `publish`).\n\n- **First publish:** the table is empty, so `similar == []` and the item has no\n  floats. It succeeds (`similar=0 stored`, 201).\n- **Every later publish:** there is now at least one existing story, so\n  `similar` has a float `score`. `put_item` raises `TypeError`, and `handler`\n  turns that into a 500.\n\nThe only test published a single story into an empty table, so it never\nexercised a non-empty `similar` list.\n\n## Fix (`src/app.py`)\n\n1. **At the source:** `similarity()` now returns\n   `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`. Going through `str` gives an exact 4-place\n   decimal such as `Decimal('0.4429')`, not the float's binary expansion.\n   Sorting and comparing still work as before.\n2. **At the write boundary, so it can't come back:** a new `to_dynamo()` helper\n   recursively converts any float to `Decimal`, and `publish()` sends the item\n   through it right before `put_item`. A float added to the item later (a new\n   field, a changed formula) gets converted instead of causing another 500.\n\n## Regression tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_float_free_scores`: publishes two related\n  stories and checks the second one stores with a non-empty `similar`. This is\n  the exact production failure.\n- `test_handler_returns_201_for_every_publish`: five publishes through\n  `handler`, and each one must return 201.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_nested_floats`: checks the boundary helper on\n  nested dicts and lists.\n\n`tests/fake_dynamo.py` already rejects floats the same way boto3 does. Before\nthe fix the new tests fail with that `TypeError`; after it, all 4 tests pass\n(`python3 -m unittest discover tests`).\n\n## Side note (not the cause of this bug)\n\n`table.scan()` returns at most 1 MB per call, and `publish` doesn't follow\n`LastEvaluatedKey`. Once the library is large, `similar` will be computed from\nonly part of it. This won't cause a 500, but it's worth paginating (or\nprecomputing) later.\n"}}}
