ession tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_float_free_scores`: publishes two related\n  stories and checks the second one stores with a non-empty `similar`. This is\n  the exact production failure.\n- `test_handler_returns_201_for_every_publish`: five publishes through\n  `handler`, and each one must return 201.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_nested_floats`: checks the boundary helper on\n  nested dicts and lists.\n\n`tests/fake_dynamo.py` already rejects floats the same way boto3 does. Before\nthe fix the new tests fail with that `TypeError`; after it, all 4 tests pass\n(`python3 -m unittest discover tests`).\n\n## Side note (not the cause of this bug)\n\n`table.scan()` returns at most 1 MB per call, and `publish` doesn't follow\n`LastEvaluatedKey`. Once the library is large, `similar` will be computed from\nonly part of it. This won't cause a 500, but it's worth paginating (or\nprecomputing) later.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MTS9yWqbkz76qWxhytbtD2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSDmUHPanEfosmhBNWbz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the second-publish 500, and the cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Cause:** each stored story includes its three most similar stories, each with a `score`. `similarity()` returned that score as a Python `float`, and DynamoDB (through boto3) rejects floats with `TypeError: Float types are not supported`. The first publish worked only because the table was empty, so the similar-stories list had no scores in it. Every publish after that includes a float score, so writing the item fails and the handler returns 500. The one existing test only ever published into an empty table, so it never hit this.\n\n**Fix (`src/app.py`):**\n- `similarity()` now returns an exact `Decimal` instead of a float.\n- A new `to_dynamo()` function converts any float anywhere in the item to `Decimal`, and `publish()` runs every item through it just before writing. If someone adds a float field later, it gets converted instead of causing another 500.\n\n**Tests:** I added three regression tests to `tests/test_publish.py`. One publishes two related stories, which is the exact production failure. One sends five publishes through the handler and requires a 201 each time. One checks `to_dynamo()` on nested data. They fail on the old code and all 4 tests pass with the fix.\n\n**Separate issue, not fixed:** `publish()` reads only the first page of the table scan (DynamoDB returns at most 1 MB per scan call). Once the library gets big, similar stories will be picked from only part of it. It won't cause errors, but it's worth fixing later.\n\nNothing was committed or deployed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1115,"cache_read_input_tokens":26579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1115},"output_tokens":517,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27d8ba11-6068-4a90-8ad8-f7dd4035c154","uuid":"ca8657cf-69cb-4718-8817-2db17a4b9543","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:52:14.881Z","request_id":"req_011CgSDmTu52jJYyc2EJo24o"}
